course: dictionary
lesson: 13728
title: A tough outer covering
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from science, and you will meet them in biology books. Context still helps, because the words around a new word leave clues. «Your skin is an integument that covers your whole body.» Skin covers and protects you, so an integument must be a covering.
explain: The word is about covering and protecting. «The seed's integument kept the baby plant safe until it was ready to grow.» A seed needs a tough outer coat, so integument must mean a tough outer layer. Swap in the word covering and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Scientists also use the phrase the integumentary system. It is said in-TEG-yoo-MEN-tar-ee, and it means your skin, hair and nails. Once you know the word integument, the longer phrase is much easier to understand.
fact: Integument means a tough outer layer or covering.
fact: Plants and animals both can have an integument.
fact: Examples of integuments are skin, a shell, a husk and the coat of a seed.
fact: The integumentary system is skin, hair and nails.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word covering and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The seed's integument kept the baby plant safe.» What is an integument? | *A tough outer covering | A kind of rock | A sweet juice inside a fruit | A root that grows down into the soil
exercise: What does the integumentary system include? | Leaves, roots and stems | Bones, muscles and blood | *Skin, hair and nails | Teeth, tongue and eyes
exercise: «Your skin is an integument that covers your whole body.» Find and copy the word that tells you what an integument does. | skin | *covers | integument | body
test: «A hard shell is an integument.» What does integument mean? | A moving part of a machine | A hard bone inside the body | A type of food | *A tough outer layer or covering
test: The integumentary system is made of which three things? | Brain, heart and eyes | Leaves, stems and flowers | Blood, bones and lungs | *Skin, hair and nails
exam: Which of these is an example of an integument? | A stone path | A drop of water | A loud noise | *The coat of a bean seed
